        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): tighten grepSchema context/limit from Type.Number to Type.Integer",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: `grepSchema.context` and `grepSchema.limit` in `src/agents/sessions/tools/grep.ts` accept floating-point values via `Type.Number()`, while both fields represent integer semantics — context lines and match count. A float value (e.g. `context=1.5`) could silently truncate, giving unexpected results.\n\n**Solution**: Tighten both `context` and `limit` to `Type.Integer()` — matching the pattern already applied to sibling tool schemas (`read.ts`, `find.ts`, `ls.ts`). TypeBox rejects float values at the parameter parsing stage.\n\n**What changed**: Two `Type.Number()` → `Type.Integer()` replacements in `grep.ts`. No runtime logic changes. No config, CLI, or public API surface changed.\n\n**merge-risk declaration**: No — schema-only change to an internal tool schema type. No session state, auth, message delivery, or security boundary involved.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Schema-level rejection of float values for `context` and `limit` in the grep tool. Type.Integer enforces integer-only input at parameter parsing time.\n\n**Real environment tested**: Linux x86_64 (local workstation)\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**: `pnpm build:ci-artifacts` → exit 0\n\n**After-fix evidence**: TypeScript compilation succeeds with the updated schema types. The `pnpm build:ci-artifacts` target confirms the source is syntactically and semantically valid.\n\n**Observed result after the fix**: Build passes cleanly. The schema change is validated at compile time (Type.Integer is a valid TypeBox schema type accepted by TypeScript's type checker).\n\n**What was not tested**: End-to-end LLM grep tool invocation through the Gateway runtime. The schema type change compiles and is type-safe; runtime behavior change (float rejection) is enforced by TypeBox's Value.Check at tool-call time.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `pnpm build:ci-artifacts` → exit 0 ✓ (compilation succeeds with updated schema type)\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible — existing callers passing integer values work identically; callers passing floats now get a clear validation error at schema level\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations — built successfully with default config\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation — not needed, internal tool schema change\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary — no breaking changes\n",
        "branch": "fix/scan-20260713-7-grep-type-integer",
